# Classical theta-one proof notice

These short wrappers were prepared for QuasiRiemannTracker PR #5 with AI
assistance on 12 October 2026. They apply established Mathlib theorems and are
distributed under Apache-2.0; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).

The imported Mathlib development is pinned to commit
`d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612`.

- `Mathlib/NumberTheory/LSeries/Dirichlet.lean`: copyright 2024 Michael Stoll;
  author Michael Stoll. This supplies the Dirichlet-series and Riemann-zeta
  nonvanishing theorems in the half-plane `1 < re s`.
- `Mathlib/NumberTheory/LSeries/DirichletContinuation.lean`: copyright 2024
  David Loeffler; authors David Loeffler and Michael Stoll. This identifies the
  analytically continued Dirichlet L-function with its convergent series.

Mathlib's imported dependencies retain their original notices and licenses.
These wrappers express the classical Euler-product bound.

Restored historical submissions

The Lean sources for Akash Levy's weighted numerator, Argonaut's perturbed
boundary, Baiying Liu's optimized parameters, Hailey Collet's Cycle25 quartic
endpoint, ProofCouncil's QRH proof, and nielstron's rational and algebraic
revisions are retained under submissions/. Original author notices in the Lean
files are preserved. Each submission's metadata identifies the original source
and verification evidence. The restoration relocates module imports beneath
Candidate and adds the standard Candidate.bound wrapper; theorem bodies and
declaration namespaces are retained.

Akash Levy's WeightedQRH sources retain their original declarations and proof
bodies. Their OAI imports use the project's pinned OpenAI dependency.

Shared submission modules

Supporting modules use Submissions.<result_id> paths, with hyphens replaced by
underscores. Identical modules with identical transitive import closures are
reused from an earlier source revision through metadata dependencies. Source
notices and author credits are retained. Candidate.Main exports each result's
bound from its reusable submission module.


